WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.570 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  like many Greek villages Morris is  mostly old they were preparing for a  funeral when we arrived but in this  village of 600 people they have other  worries than the dead in the hotel over  the railway line 400 refugees are being  housed it isn't going well the first  time I saw them I felt fear I saw faces  full of anger I could see them thinking  that I was safe in my house why are we  suffering is to keep my daughter's  bicycle outside but one of them tried to  take it they've got a nerve they don't  understand anything the other day the  villagers met and told the police they  were feeling unprotected and said they  were thinking about arming themselves  with guns against the refugees obviously  everyone has to do something and if we  don't have a weapon we'll find something  else at the hotel they know all about  this but it's not their main problem  there's a mental health crisis to  contend with I share the same took us to  the place where a few days ago an Afghan  man who'd been wrongly told his wife and  children had been moved somewhere else  without him hanged himself from a tree  the next day Hussein's friend riad  hanged himself inside the hotel  his entire family had been killed in  Iraq he complained his severe depression  was being ignored his funeral wasn't  quite so well attended as the one in the  village he told them what had happened  to his family they gave him an injection  and he was like a robot when he came  back he was saying everyday I'm not okay  I'm not okay and they did nothing for  him over the last few months the  incoming center-right Greek government  has scaled back medical and psychiatric  support for Refugees to prove to an  increasingly hostile public that it's on  their side here they can bandage their  feet  not their minds now a lot of people are  struggling not only about mental  healthcare also when they need an  operation that follow up after  operations x-rays seems like this or as  it's much more difficult to find a place  where the people get treatment the sad  truth is that the story of Morris is in  microcosm a reflection of how Europe has  failed to get on top of refugee  resettlements and to heal people even in  hospitable Greece these two groups of  people are worlds apart  Lawrence Lee al-jazeera Maurice northern  Greece

